t automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1772,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[752,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[735,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1018,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[738,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1052,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1057,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1168,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[2036,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[2037,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[2035,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[952,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1028,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[506,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[673,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[672,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[303,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1124,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1178,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1338,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1177,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1337,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1734,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1733,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[848,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1577,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1654,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[986,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1627,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[474,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[944,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[588,"`slot=\