ns or submit forms with a single click"],[538,"The button's accessible name is built from two sources, combined in order:"],[188,"The Carousel component allows users to cycle through a series of content panels (typically images, cards, or text) in a horizontal or vertical layout. It is commonly used for featured content, product showcases, or testimonials."],[208,"The carousel follows the current **layout direction** (LTR or RTL). By default, that direction is detected automatically from the browser or system settings."],[2033,"The chart follows the current layout direction, normally detected from the browser or system settings. In right-to-left it mirrors the axes and labels; this example forces RTL so you can see it in a left-to-right page."],[1873,"The chart follows the current layout direction, which is normally detected from the browser or system settings. In right-to-left it mirrors the axes, bars, and labels; this example forces RTL so you can see it in a left-to-right page. RTL support is still being refined - axis rendering and tick spacing in particular."],[2039,"The chart root exposes data attributes that reflect prop state for styling:"],[1547,"The colored dot is decorative and invisible to screen readers. The text label must convey the status on its own — never rely on the dot alone to communicate meaning."],[662,"The component accepts standard `className` and `style` props:"],[671,"The component also includes accessibility attributes:"],[664,"The component automatically adds data attributes for styling hooks:"],[1508,"The component exposes state through data attributes:"],[639,"The component extends `BentoIconProps` and passes through all standard HTML attributes and accessibility props to the underlying Bento Icon component. This includes:"],[2044,"The component sets ARIA attributes on interactive and structural elements as needed."],[1962,"The component uses `container-type: inline-size` and fills its parent width. Ensure the parent has a defined wid